coring-agent.fingerprint\n   687→        scope: backend/synthetics/fingerprint.py — compute_fingerprint(digest, contract)\n   688→          produces stable JSON per candidate\n   689→      - id: synthetics-scoring-agent.diff\n   690→        scope: backend/synthetics/diff.py — diff_against_baseline(fingerprint, baseline,\n   691→          contract) returns DriftReport\n   692→      - id: synthetics-scoring-agent.cli\n   693→        scope: backend/synthetics/cli.py — python -m backend.synthetics run\n   694→          --suite=scoring\n   695→      - id: synthetics-scoring-agent.cache-verification\n   696→        scope: backend/synthetics/scoring_runner.py — verify cache_creation_input_tokens\n   697→          == 0 on subsequent runs\n   698→  - id: synthetics-crawler-agent\n   699→    scope: Upstream health monitoring with state machine alerts for consecutive\n   700→      failures\n   701→    branch: feat/synthetics-crawler-agent\n   702→    blocked_by:\n   703→      - synthetics-fixtures-agent\n   704→    blocks: []\n   705→    capabilities:\n   706→      - httpx\n   707→      - redis-pubsub\n   708→      - structlog\n   709→    sub_agents:\n   710→      - id: synthetics-crawler-agent.runner\n   711→        scope: backend/synthetics/crawler_health.py — CrawlerHealthRunner.run_suite()\n   712→          hits known-good slugs per source\n   713→      - id: synthetics-crawler-agent.schemas\n   714→        scope: backend/synthetics/expected_schema_v1.json — expected top-level shape for\n   715→          Greenhouse/Lever/Ashby\n   716→      - id: synthetics-crawler-agent.state-machine\n   717→        scope: synthetics/state.json — consecutive_failures tracking with 3-strike alert\n   718→          threshold\n   719→      - id: synthetics-crawler-agent.beat-extension\n   720→        scope: backend/synthetics/beat_schedule.py — hourly Celery beat entry for\n   721→          crawler health, registered additively\n   722→merge_order:\n   723→  - data-agent\n   724→  - design-agent\n   725→  - auth-agent\n   726→  - obs-agent\n   727→  - discover-agent\n   728→  - apply-agent\n   729→  - agents-agent\n   730→  - api-agent\n   731→  - scheduler-agent\n   732→  - api-streaming-agent\n   733→  - frontend-agent\n   734→  - api-client-agent\n   735→  - infra-agent\n   736→  - tests-agent\n   737→  - synthetics-fixtures-agent\n   738→  - synthetics-scoring-agent\n   739→  - synthetics-crawler-agent\n   740→timeline:\n   741→  parallel_phases:\n   742→    - hours: 0-1\n   743→      active:\n   744→        - data-agent\n   745→        - design-agent\n   746→      description: Wave 1 — foundations with zero cross-biome deps. Schemas + models +\n   747→        design tokens land first so every downstream biome consumes frozen\n   748→        contracts.\n   749→    - hours: 1-3\n   750→      active:\n   751→        - auth-agent\n   752→        - obs-agent\n   753→      description: Wave 2 — core services depending only on data. Auth + observability\n   754→        wire on top of the schema, both consumed by every engine below.\n   755→    - hours: 3-5\n   756→      active:\n   757→        - discover-agent\n   758→      description: Wave 3a — Discovery engine with pub/sub gap closure. Must publish\n   759→        events on agent.status.discovery channel.\n   760→    - hours: 5-7\n   761→      active:\n   762→        - scheduler-agent\n   763→        - api-streaming-agent\n   764→      description: Wave 3b — Scheduler and streaming in parallel. Scheduler consumes\n   765→        discover-agent, streaming consumes obs-agent.\n   766→    - hours: 7-8\n   767→      active:\n   768→        - apply-agent\n   769→      description: Wave 4 — Application engine, blocked by discover-agent.\n   770→    - hours: 8-9\n   771→      active:\n   772→        - agents-agent\n   773→      description: Wave 5 — AgentManager wrapper over the engines.\n   774→    - hours: 9-11\n   775→      active:\n   776→        - api-agent\n   777→        - frontend-agent\n   778→     