eact-based dashboard serving 15,000+ daily active users\n      - Built RESTful APIs using Node.js and Express with PostgreSQL database integration\n      - Implemented automated testing suite achieving 85% code coverage with Jest and Cypress\n      - Collaborated with design team to improve UI/UX, reducing user support tickets by 30%\n      - Participated in Agile ceremonies including daily standups and sprint retrospectives\n\n      Junior Developer (Intern to Full-Time) | WebFlow Agency | Brooklyn, NY | Jan 2023 - May 2024\n      - Created responsive landing pages and marketing sites for 20+ small business clients\n      - Migrated legacy jQuery codebase to modern React, improving page load time by 40%\n      - Assisted senior developers in debugging production issues and optimizing database queries\n      - Wrote technical documentation for internal tools and onboarding processes\n\n      EDUCATION\n\n      Bachelor of Science in Computer Science | New York University | May 2023\n      - GPA: 3.6/4.0\n      - Relevant Coursework: Data Structures, Algorithms, Web Development, Database Systems\n      - Hackathon Winner: NYU HackNight 2022 - Built real-time collaborative note-taking app\n\n      TECHNICAL SKILLS\n\n      Languages: JavaScript, TypeScript, Python, HTML5, CSS3, SQL\n      Frontend: React, Next.js, Redux, Tailwind CSS, Material UI\n      Backend: Node.js, Express, FastAPI, REST APIs, GraphQL basics\n      Databases: PostgreSQL, MongoDB, Redis\n      Tools: Git, GitHub, Docker basics, VS Code, Figma, Jira\n      Testing: Jest, React Testing Library, Cypress\n\n      PROJECTS\n\n      TaskFlow - Personal Project Management App (github.com/jchen-dev/taskflow)\n      - Built full-stack task management app with React frontend and Node.js backend\n      - Implemented real-time updates using WebSockets for collaborative features\n      - Deployed on Vercel (frontend) and Railway (backend) with CI/CD via GitHub Actions\n\n      WeatherNow - React Native Mobile App\n      - Developed cross-platform weather app using React Native and OpenWeatherMap API\n      - Implemented location-based weather with push notifications for severe weather alerts\n\n      CERTIFICATIONS\n      - AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner (2024)\n      - Meta Front-End Developer Professional Certificate (2023)\n\n  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  # SYNTHETIC-SENIOR-ML\n  # Staff-level ML engineer, 8+ years experience\n  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  - slug: synthetic-senior-ml\n    name: Dr. Priya Ramanathan\n    email: priya.ramanathan.synthetic@talent-agent.test\n    identity_context:\n      location: San Francisco, CA\n      target_salary_min: 250000\n      target_salary_max: 350000\n      remote_preference: remote_only\n      experience_years: 9\n      leadership_level: Staff\n    target_locations:\n      - San Francisco, CA\n      - Remote\n    excluded_companies:\n      - Oracle\n      - IBM\n    excluded_industries:\n      - Oil and Gas\n      - Tobacco\n    resume_text: |\n      DR. PRIYA RAMANATHAN\n      Staff Machine Learning Engineer\n      San Francisco, CA | priya.ram@email.com | linkedin.com/in/priyaram | github.com/priya-ml\n\n      SUMMARY\n      Staff-level ML engineer with 9 years of experience building production ML systems at\n      scale. Expert in deep learning, distributed training, and MLOps infrastructure.\n      Published researcher with 12 peer-reviewed papers. Proven track record of leading\n      cross-functional teams and delivering ML products used by millions of users.\n\n      EXPERIENCE\n\n      Staff Machine Learning Engineer | Anthropic | San Francisco, CA | March 2022 - Present\n      - Lead technical direction for retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) infrastructure\n      - Architected distributed training pipeline processing 500TB+ of text data monthly\n      - Reduced model inference latency by 60% through quantization and caching optimizations\n      - Mentored team of 6 ML engineers, establishing best practices for experiment tracking\n      - Collaborated with research team on novel attention mechanisms for long-context models\n\n      Senior Machine Learning Engineer | Scale AI | San Francisco, CA | Jan 2019 - Feb 2022\n      - Built data labeling quality assurance system using active learning, improving label\n        accuracy from 92% to 98.5%\n      - Designed and deployed computer vision pipeline for autonomous vehicle annotation\n      - Led migration from TensorFlow 1.x to PyTorch, reducing training time by 35%\n      - Authored internal course on MLOps best practices, trained 50+ engineers\n\n      Machine Learning Engineer | Uber ATG | Pittsburgh, PA | Aug 2016 - Dec 2018\n      - Developed real-time object detection models for self-driving vehicles\n      - Implemented distributed training infrastructure using Horovod across 128 GPUs\n      - Built A/B testing framework for ML model deployment with statistical rigor\n      - Published research on domain adaptation for weather-robust perception systems\n\n      Research Scientist Intern | Google Brain | Mountain View, CA | Summer 2015\n      - Researched attention mechanisms for sequence-to-sequence models\n      - Contributed to TensorFlow open-source project (2 merged PRs)\n\n      EDUCATION\n\n      Ph.D. in Computer Science (Machine Learning) | Carnegie Mellon University | 2016\n      - Dissertation: \"Efficient Deep Learning for Resource-Constrained Environments\"\n      - Advisor: Dr. Geoffrey Hinton (visiting), Dr. Ruslan Salakhutdinov\n      - NSF Graduate Research Fellowship\n\n      M.S. in Computer Science | Stanford University | 2012\n      - Focus: Artificial Intelligence and Natural Language Processing\n\n      B.Tech in Computer Science | IIT Bombay | 2010\n      - Gold Medalist, Department of Computer Science\n\n      TECHNICAL SKILLS\n\n      Languages: Python, C++, CUDA, SQL, Rust (learning)\n      ML Frameworks: PyTorch, TensorFlow, JAX, Hugging Face Transformers\n      Infrastructure: Kubernetes, Ray, Spark, Airflow, MLflow, Weights & Biases\n      Cloud: AWS (SageMaker, EKS, S3), GCP (Vertex AI, TPU), Azure ML\n      Specializations: LLMs, RAG systems, distributed training, model optimization,\n        computer vision, NLP, MLOps\n\n      PUBLICATIONS (Selected)\n\n      - \"Efficient Attention Mechanisms for Long-Context Language Models\" - NeurIPS 2023\n      - \"Domain Adaptation for Robust Perception in Adverse Weather\" - CVPR 2018\n      - \"Active Learning for Data-Efficient Model Training\" - ICML 2020\n      - 9 additional peer-reviewed publications (Google Scholar: 2,400+ citations)\n\n      PATENTS\n      - US Patent 11,234,567: \"Method for Efficient Inference in Transformer Models\"\n      - US Patent 10,987,654: \"System for Automated ML Pipeline Orchestration\"\n\n      SPEAKING\n      - NeurIPS 2023: Workshop on Efficient Deep Learning\n      - PyTorch Conference 2022: Distributed Training at Scale\n      - MLOps Community Summit 2021: Building Reliable ML Systems\n\n  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  # SYNTHETIC-MID-PRODUCT\n  # Senior product manager, 5 years experience\n  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  - slug: synthetic-mid-product\n    name: Marcus Thompson\n    email: marcus.thompson.synthetic@talent-agent.test\n    identity_context:\n      location: Austin, TX\n      target_salary_min: 150000\n      target_salary_max: 200000\n      remote_preference: remote_only\n      experience_years: 5\n      leadership_level: Manager\n    target_locations:\n      - Austin, TX\n      - Remote\n    excluded_companies:\n      - Amazon\n      - Uber\n    excluded_industries:\n      - Crypto\n      - Adult Entertainment\n    resume_text: |\n      MARCUS THOMPSON\n      Senior Product Manager\n      Austin, TX | marcus.t@email.com | linkedin.com/in/marcusthompson\n\n      SUMMARY\n      Data-driven product manager with 5 years of experience building B2B SaaS products\n      that customers love. Skilled at translating complex technical capabilities into\n      compelling user experiences. Track record of launching products that drive measurable\n      business outcomes. Passionate about the intersection of technology and human needs.\n\n      EXPERIENCE\n\n      Senior Product Manager | Notion | Austin, TX (Remote) | Jan 2022 - Present\n      - Own product roadmap for Notion's collaboration features serving 30M+ users\n      - Led launch of real-time commenting system, driving 25% increase in team adoption\n      - Partnered with engineering to reduce page load time by 40%, improving NPS by 15 points\n      - Conducted 100+ customer interviews to identify pain points in enterprise workflows\n      - Managed cross-functional team of 8 engineers, 2 designers, and 1 researcher\n      - Defined and tracked OKRs, achieving 90%+ goal completion for 6 consecutive quarters\n\n      Product Manager | Figma | San Francisco, CA | June 2020 - Dec 2021\n      - Launched Figma's component library feature, adopted by 60% of enterprise customers\n      - Built product analytics infrastructure using Amplitude and Mixpanel\n      - Created experimentation framework enabling 3x more A/B tests per quarter\n      - Collaborated with sales team to close $2M in enterprise deals through product demos\n\n      Associate Product Manager | Atlassian | Austin, TX | Aug 2019 - May 2020\n      - Shipped 5 features for Jira's agile board, improving sprint planning efficiency\n      - Analyzed user behavior data to identify and fix top 3 workflow friction points\n      - Wrote PRDs and user stories for engineering team of 6 developers\n\n      Business Analyst | Deloitte Consulting | Houston, TX | July 2017 - July 2019\n      - Advised Fortune 500 clients on digital transformation strategy\n      - Built financial models for technology investment decisions\n      - Led requirements gathering workshops for enterprise software implementations\n\n      EDUCATION\n\n      MBA | McCombs School of Business, UT Austin | 2019\n      - Concentration: Technology Commercialization\n      - Product Management Club President\n\n      B.S. in Economics | Rice University | 2017\n      - Minor: Computer Science\n      - Cum Laude\n\n      SKILLS\n\n      Product: Roadmapping, user research, A/B testing, analytics, pricing strategy,\n        go-to-market planning, competitive analysis\n      Tools: Figma, Notion, Jira, Amplitude, Mixpanel, Looker, SQL, Python (basic),\n        Miro, Dovetail\n      Methodologies: Agile, Scrum, Jobs-to-be-Done, Design Thinking, OKRs\n      Domain: B2B SaaS, collaboration tools, productivity software, developer tools\n\n      CERTIFICATIONS\n      - Pragmatic Institute Certified Product Manager\n      - Google Analytics Certified\n      - Reforge Product Strategy Program (2023)\n\n      ACHIEVEMENTS\n      - Product Hunt: #3 Product of the Day for Notion real-time features launch\n      - Speaker at ProductCon Austin 2023: \"Building Products for the Async Workforce\"\n      - Featured in First Round Review: \"How We Prioritize Features at Notion\"\n\n      INTERESTS\n      - Angel investor in 3 early-stage B2B SaaS startups\n      - Mentor at Austin Product Meetup\n      - Avid rock climber and amateur coffee roaster\n","numLines":286,"startLine":1,"totalLines":286}}}}
