{"t":"2026-05-28T03:40:31.463Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01HB2LNU4FMNr8jMC3kahEKP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have all the context. My scope is `backend/synthetics/scoring_runner.py — ScoringSyntheticRunner.run_suite() iterates synthetic candidates × JDs`. \n\nI need to create:\n1. `backend/synthetics/__init__.py` — module init (if not exists)\n2. `backend/synthetics/scoring_runner.py` — The runner that iterates synthetic candidates × JDs\n\nThe runner will:\n1. Load synthetic candidates from the database (WHERE id::text LIKE '00000000-%')\n2. Load JD fixtures from `synthetics/fixtures/jobs/`\n3. For each candidate × JD pair, call `RelevanceScorer.score_job()` with cache_control instrumentation\n4. Track cache hit/miss from response usage\n5. Return scored jobs for fingerprinting\n\nThe HYPHA states the scorer module is FROZEN. If it doesn't support cache_control, I must either call Claude directly or wrap with instrumentation. Looking at the scorer, it does NOT use cache_control — so I need to wrap the calls.\n\nLet me now write the `scoring_runner.py`:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":349,"cache_read_input_tokens":92068,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":349,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a09f4fa-29b0-40d4-99d3-86bdcfeef6a7","uuid":"2193850d-df2a-4eea-8a0b-80f6d6caedc1"}}
